      "side": 1,
      "message": "Vinh brought this up as well. dylibs themselves set `LOCAL_DYLIB_LIBRARIES` to point to their transitive dylib deps, and make walks the `LOCAL_DYLIB_LIBRARIES` links recursively. And an rlib cannot link to a dylib in soong (except the stdlib). These two reasons make dylibs not a problem.\n\nrlibs can link to cc shared libraries though.\n\nI think that means we could also fix this problem by making make walk `LOCAL_RLIB_LIBRARIES` to look for more `LOCAL_SHARED_LIBRARIES`. But it would be the first instance of walking some deps without actually installing them as shared libraries.",
